It's bitter.

724
00:31:21,797 --> 00:31:23,423
-I've decided.
-[Machu] So have I.

725
00:31:23,507 --> 00:31:24,925
-Ready, go.
-Ready, go.

726
00:31:25,842 --> 00:31:27,052
Ooh!

727
00:31:27,844 --> 00:31:29,262
[Shime] That's decisive.

728
00:31:29,346 --> 00:31:30,430
Then, Umi.

729
00:31:30,514 --> 00:31:31,807
[Machu] For Noel…

730
00:31:32,474 --> 00:31:33,725
Now imagine you're Noel.

731
00:31:38,522 --> 00:31:40,440
[chuckles] What?

732
00:31:40,524 --> 00:31:42,567
Nope, it's not him. I don't see it.

733
00:31:42,651 --> 00:31:45,904
Since we came all this way,
let's pick a flavor he'd never expect.

734
00:31:45,987 --> 00:31:47,739
[Genta] Exactly, you read my mind.

735
00:31:47,823 --> 00:31:49,533
[in English] So, do you have…

736
00:31:50,408 --> 00:31:53,411
So, not a sweetie.

737
00:31:53,495 --> 00:31:55,080
-No sweet.
-[server] Okay. All right, yeah.

738
00:31:55,163 --> 00:31:57,666
So you want something
that's not super sweet.

739
00:31:57,749 --> 00:31:59,668
Do you want it to still be like an IPA?

740
00:31:59,751 --> 00:32:00,752
-Yes.
-[Machu] Yeah.

741
00:32:00,836 --> 00:32:02,420
[server] Okay.
Let me see what I can find for you.

742
00:32:02,504 --> 00:32:03,922
-Thank you so much.
-Thank you so much.

743
00:32:04,005 --> 00:32:05,340
Thank you.

744
00:32:05,423 --> 00:32:06,424
-[in Japanese] How kind.
-Right?

745
00:32:06,508 --> 00:32:07,509
[Machu] So kind.

746
00:32:08,051 --> 00:32:09,386
-[server] All right.
-[Genta] Oh, yeah.

747
00:32:09,469 --> 00:32:10,804
-[Machu] All right. All right.
-[Genta] Wow.

748
00:32:10,887 --> 00:32:11,930
[server] So, here I…

749
00:32:12,013 --> 00:32:13,849
-Since you're in the Southwest…
-[Machu] Uh-huh.

750
00:32:13,932 --> 00:32:15,809
[server] …you've got to try
the Southwest Coast IPA.

751
00:32:15,892 --> 00:32:17,060
-[Machu] Okay.
-[Genta] Yeah, yeah.

752
00:32:17,144 --> 00:32:22,774
[server] This one is a little less sweet
and we brewed it specifically to pair with

753
00:32:22,858 --> 00:32:25,735
all of the fun stuff you can
get up to in the Southwest.

754
00:32:25,819 --> 00:32:26,820
-Nice.
-Okay.

755
00:32:26,903 --> 00:32:28,697
-[server] Yeah. Enjoy.
-I can try.

756
00:32:28,780 --> 00:32:30,115
-Thank you.
-Thank you so much.

757
00:32:30,198 --> 00:32:31,199
-[server] Yeah.
-Thank you.

758
00:32:34,703 --> 00:32:35,704
Oh.

759
00:32:37,247 --> 00:32:38,373
[in Japanese] It's good.

760
00:32:39,541 --> 00:32:41,001
[Genta] Wait, I'm kinda liking this one.

761
00:32:44,337 --> 00:32:45,172
It goes down easy.

762
00:32:45,255 --> 00:32:46,548
Light and easy, right?

763
00:32:49,634 --> 00:32:50,635
I'm sold on this one.

764
00:32:50,719 --> 00:32:52,554
-I think Noel will like it too.
-[Genta] Yeah.

765
00:32:52,637 --> 00:32:54,306
-Let's do that then.
-[Machu] Nice, nice, nice.

766
00:32:54,389 --> 00:32:55,557
We've made our picks.

767
00:32:59,686 --> 00:33:01,438
[Shime] Think they'll like it?

768
00:33:01,521 --> 00:33:03,190
We bought a ton of souvenirs.

769
00:33:03,273 --> 00:33:04,649
-I won't deny that.
-True.

770
00:33:04,733 --> 00:33:06,568
We got these drinks and the necklace.

771
00:33:06,651 --> 00:33:08,570
-True. That's so true.
-Right?

772
00:33:08,653 --> 00:33:09,654
I'm super excited.

773
00:33:09,738 --> 00:33:11,198
-[in English] All right, I might…
-Here comes!

774
00:33:11,281 --> 00:33:12,782
-I might be missing one.
-Thank you.

775
00:33:12,866 --> 00:33:14,659
-Yeah.
-Okay.

776
00:33:14,743 --> 00:33:17,621
So I have the Southwest Coast IPA.

777
00:33:17,704 --> 00:33:18,705
-Okay.
-Yeah.

778
00:33:18,788 --> 00:33:20,665
Mexi Style Cold IPA.

779
00:33:20,749 --> 00:33:23,043
-Okay.
-The Checkered Future IPA.

780
00:33:23,126 --> 00:33:23,960
-Okay.
-Yeah.

781
00:33:24,044 --> 00:33:26,463
-Hazy IPA, that's the one.
-Hazy IPA.

782
00:33:26,546 --> 00:33:29,049
And then I have this
delicious lemon Skagua.

783
00:33:29,716 --> 00:33:31,468
[in Japanese]
We're grabbing two just for Shizuya.

784
00:33:31,551 --> 00:33:32,886
[Genta] These two for Shizuya.

785
00:33:32,969 --> 00:33:34,054
-This one.
-This one.

786
00:33:35,305 --> 00:33:36,890
-All right.
-That's the whole set.

787
00:33:36,973 --> 00:33:38,850
-Heck, yeah.
-[in English] We are Travis Japan!

788
00:33:38,934 --> 00:33:41,061
-Travis Japan!
-[in Japanese] There we go!

789
00:33:41,144 --> 00:33:43,271
-Don't you think they'll love it?
-They'll definitely be so happy.

790
00:33:43,355 --> 00:33:44,189
I love the design.

791
00:33:44,272 --> 00:33:45,273
-It's cute.
-Right?

792
00:33:48,443 --> 00:33:49,945
You guys are gonna explore the town, yeah?

793
00:33:50,028 --> 00:33:52,405
I thought it'd be fun to go shop around.

794
00:33:52,489 --> 00:33:55,617
I'm ready to go chill.
I'm kinda in the mood to chill now.

795
00:33:55,700 --> 00:33:57,452
-Are you going back to the hotel?
-Got it, okay.

796
00:33:57,535 --> 00:33:58,995
-Yeah.
-[Shime] All right, see ya later.

797
00:33:59,079 --> 00:34:00,163
Which way are we going?

798
00:34:00,247 --> 00:34:01,456
-[Shime] If it works out then.
-Bye now.

799
00:34:01,539 --> 00:34:04,125
-[Machu] He'll definitely flake on us.
-[Shime] Okay, well, enjoy your rest.

800
00:34:04,209 --> 00:34:05,377
[Genta] Yeah.

801
00:34:05,460 --> 00:34:07,337
-See ya.
-[Genta] See you later.

802
00:34:07,879 --> 00:34:14,344
All right, it's time for me to enjoy
some alone time at the hotel.

803
00:34:14,928 --> 00:34:16,471
This hotel is incredible.

804
00:34:22,185 --> 00:34:23,186
You see this?

805
00:34:24,187 --> 00:34:25,188
This place is amazing, huh?

806
00:34:25,272 --> 00:34:30,652
I can access my room
without taking the elevator.

807
00:34:30,735 --> 00:34:32,112
Just climb up

808
00:34:33,363 --> 00:34:34,781
a flight of stairs.

809
00:34:37,158 --> 00:34:39,160
Here I am.

810
00:34:39,244 --> 00:34:41,079
Room 220.

811
00:34:43,790 --> 00:34:47,168
Seriously,
those two never run out of energy.

812
00:34:47,794 --> 00:34:48,795
The key…

813
00:34:49,421 --> 00:34:51,214
Time to whip out my key.

814
00:34:55,135 --> 00:34:57,554
Welcome to Matsuda's suite!

815
00:34:58,179 --> 00:34:59,472
Isn't it amazing?

816
00:35:03,101 --> 00:35:05,520
Apparently, this room…

817
00:35:07,689 --> 00:35:10,775
is even featured on a book
about this hotel.

818
00:35:10,859 --> 00:35:12,485
This room's special…

819
00:35:13,194 --> 00:35:16,448
Apparently,
it's special for one reason or another.

820
00:35:20,035 --> 00:35:21,244
Finally, we're here.

821
00:35:23,580 --> 00:35:24,956
Here we are.

822
00:35:25,040 --> 00:35:26,124
[light switch clicks]

823
00:35:31,504 --> 00:35:32,922
[water running]

824
00:35:35,967 --> 00:35:37,636
I'm growing a 'stache.

825
00:35:39,804 --> 00:35:43,683
I'm not shaving once this trip.

826
00:35:43,767 --> 00:35:49,314
Even just being out in the sun
saps my energy.

827
00:35:52,359 --> 00:35:54,069
Right, right?

828
00:35:55,487 --> 00:35:57,822
You can't beat this relaxation.

829
00:35:58,657 --> 00:36:00,492
I'm gonna relax.

830
00:36:01,368 --> 00:36:03,370
It's time for me to rest, guys.

831
00:36:05,163 --> 00:36:07,290
I'm tapping out, yeah.

832
00:36:08,249 --> 00:36:09,876
That picture right there…

833
00:36:09,959 --> 00:36:11,711
that picture's always, like,

834
00:36:11,795 --> 00:36:15,882
looking at me when I'm on the bed.

835
00:36:16,716 --> 00:36:20,011
It sits dead center in my view.

836
00:36:20,887 --> 00:36:23,014
It's a little creepy, don't you think?

837
00:36:24,808 --> 00:36:27,560
And look at this one too.

838
00:36:27,644 --> 00:36:31,856
You can see the reflection
of the bed on that mirror.

839
00:36:33,733 --> 00:36:35,318
It's creepier than you'd expect.

840
00:36:37,696 --> 00:36:38,697
All right.

841
00:36:38,780 --> 00:36:41,825
Seriously, guys,
it's time for me to get some rest.

842
00:36:41,908 --> 00:36:43,159
Bye-bye!

843
00:36:46,246 --> 00:36:48,665
[narrator]
After recharging with a power nap,

844
00:36:48,748 --> 00:36:51,501
Genta joined Shime and Machu,
who have returned from exploring the town,

845
00:36:51,584 --> 00:36:53,461
at the saloon located on
the hotel basement floor.

846
00:36:53,545 --> 00:36:54,796
[Shime] Awesome.

847
00:36:54,879 --> 00:36:58,007
[narrator] The bar exudes a quiet luxury,
steeped in the Old Frontier charm.

848
00:37:00,385 --> 00:37:02,470
[♪ blues music plays]

849
00:37:02,554 --> 00:37:03,596
[in English] Hello.

850
00:37:03,680 --> 00:37:04,723
-Hello.
-Hello. How are ya?

851
00:37:04,806 --> 00:37:06,891
-Great.
-We are pretty good.

852
00:37:06,975 --> 00:37:08,643
-Thank you.
-I'm just gonna give menus for y'all.

853
00:37:08,727 --> 00:37:09,894
-Thanks so much.
-Thank you so much.

854
00:37:09,978 --> 00:37:11,146
Yeah, of course.

855
00:37:11,229 --> 00:37:13,773
Do you have local beer?

856
00:37:13,857 --> 00:37:17,277
We do. Yeah, we have
a Mexican lager and a hazy IPA.

857
00:37:17,360 --> 00:37:18,695
Ah, okay. Uh…

858
00:37:18,778 --> 00:37:19,904
You wanna try one of those?

859
00:37:19,988 --> 00:37:21,865
-Yes.
-Yeah, I recommend the Mexican lager.

860
00:37:21,948 --> 00:37:23,950
-Yes. Yes, please.
-Perfect.

861
00:37:24,033 --> 00:37:26,327
Two Mexican beer and…

862
00:37:26,411 --> 00:37:27,996
-Orange juice.
-[server] Orange juice?

863
00:37:28,079 --> 00:37:29,414
-OJ.
-OJ.

864
00:37:29,497 --> 00:37:31,833
-[server] OJ? Yeah? Absolutely.
-Yeah.

865
00:37:32,876 --> 00:37:35,211
[in Japanese]
Isn't this what Noel was talking about?

866
00:37:37,505 --> 00:37:39,507
Ah. "Know when to stop," you mean?

867
00:37:39,591 --> 00:37:41,384
-I mean, maybe.
-Like, don't black out?

868
00:37:41,468 --> 00:37:42,635
Right, don't drink too much.

869
00:37:42,719 --> 00:37:44,012
-Is that what he meant?
-Yep.

870
00:37:44,888 --> 00:37:47,140
-Oh. Good point.
-That's a great guess.

871
00:37:47,223 --> 00:37:48,892
Yeah. After all, look. The list's endless.

872
00:37:48,975 --> 00:37:50,059
[Machu] True.

873
00:37:50,143 --> 00:37:51,853
[Shime]
They've got all the alcohol in the world.

874
00:37:51,936 --> 00:37:54,606
What was it… They call it
the living museum, I think?

875
00:37:54,689 --> 00:37:55,940
-Right.
-Right.

876
00:37:56,024 --> 00:37:58,568
Durango is also
known as "The Living Museum."

877
00:37:58,651 --> 00:38:00,361
This hotel's history goes way back too.

878
00:38:00,445 --> 00:38:02,864
Just like the history
of the craft beer here.

879
00:38:02,947 --> 00:38:04,657
-True.
-Good point, good point.

880
00:38:04,741 --> 00:38:05,658
That's right.

881
00:38:05,742 --> 00:38:07,577
There must be an explanation
behind her period costume too.

882
00:38:07,660 --> 00:38:08,787
-Which one?
-Yeah, what's that about?

883
00:38:08,870 --> 00:38:10,079
We've seen all sorts of period costumes.

884
00:38:10,163 --> 00:38:11,456
[in English]
There's the orange juice for ya.

885
00:38:11,539 --> 00:38:12,749
-Thank you so much.
-Oh, yeah.

886
00:38:12,832 --> 00:38:14,334
[server] Of course, you guys.

887
00:38:14,417 --> 00:38:16,461
-[Genta] Thank you so much.
-[server] I put the french fries in.

888
00:38:16,544 --> 00:38:18,338
-[in Japanese] Shall we toast?
-Let's start with a toast.

889
00:38:18,838 --> 00:38:19,881
Ready, go.

890
00:38:19,964 --> 00:38:21,883
-Cheers.
-Cheers.

891
00:38:21,966 --> 00:38:23,635
-Cheers.
-Yes. Cheers.

892
00:38:28,807 --> 00:38:29,808
Oh!

893
00:38:30,892 --> 00:38:31,893
Yum.

894
00:38:34,521 --> 00:38:35,730
Wanna have a sip?

895
00:38:35,814 --> 00:38:37,315
Yeah, I'll take a sip.

896
00:38:38,483 --> 00:38:40,443
Lunchtime beer.

897
00:38:40,527 --> 00:38:42,278
-Beer for lunch. Great way to dine.
-This is supreme.

898
00:38:43,238 --> 00:38:44,906
-Indeed, yes.
-[Genta] It's delicious.

899
00:38:46,199 --> 00:38:47,575
[Genta] Don't force yourself to drink.

900
00:38:48,409 --> 00:38:50,495
-Just a sip, yeah?
-[Machu] It goes down easy.

901
00:38:50,578 --> 00:38:53,164
It's not bitter, but rather fruity.

902
00:38:53,248 --> 00:38:55,166
-Yeah.
-Isn't this one a Mexican beer?

903
00:38:55,250 --> 00:38:56,626
Yep, it's Mexican.

904
00:38:56,709 --> 00:38:57,961
Local beer, huh?

905
00:39:00,755 --> 00:39:04,384
Seriously, Gen-chan,
while you were waiting…

906
00:39:14,894 --> 00:39:16,271
[Noel] What'd I tell them?

907
00:39:16,354 --> 00:39:17,856
"Know when to stop!"

908
00:39:17,939 --> 00:39:19,816
I understand, though.

909
00:39:19,899 --> 00:39:23,194
Durango's craft beers are top-notch.

910
00:40:40,355 --> 00:40:42,357
Translated by Megumi Hunter
